For FFmpeg 9.0.2. Not from upstream.

Decode with VideoToolbox asynchronously: hand the session the next frame
without waiting for the one before it.

The hwaccel waited for every frame: VTDecompressionSessionDecodeFrame() with
no flags, then VTDecompressionSessionWaitForAsynchronousFrames(). The decoder
runs in another process, and with a wait after every frame it never has a
second frame to start on while the first is on its way out: 4K HEVC took
2.35 ms a frame on an M5 Max. An exact seek waits for exactly that, since it
decodes from the keyframe before its target, up to 240 frames in a film with
a keyframe every 10 seconds.

With this patch a frame is handed over with
kVTDecodeFrame_EnableAsynchronousDecompression and the call returns once the
session has taken it. The session holds the caller back by itself when it
has enough to do. The same frames then take 1.2 ms each.

  VTHWFrame            A lock, a condition and a count of the decodes the
                       session has not answered yet for this frame.
  decode_frame         Passes a reference to the frame's buffer as the
                       source frame refcon. Nothing waits.
  output callback      Finds the frame through the refcon and stores the
                       pixel buffer and its frames context in it. It used
                       to be the decoding thread that derived the frames
                       context from the pixel buffer. The callback does it
                       now, because only it knows when there is one.
  postproc_frame       Runs when the decoder returns the frame to its
                       user. Waits for the callback first.
  stop, uninit         Wait for the frames still in the session, whose
                       callbacks use the context.

A frame that fails to decode is reported when it is returned, as "No frame
decoded?", and no longer by the end_frame() of that frame.

